    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.02-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Soils matter where farming supports settlement. Productive land can attract cultivation, while households may place homes to maintain access to fields without occupying the most useful crop area. Waterlogging, erosion or thin soil can create constraints. A soil's role should be linked to the livelihood or building condition rather than merely named. Fertile soil alone does not provide transport, capital or secure land access.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-01-2",
