    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.02-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Water availability supports drinking, livestock and production. A dependable accessible source can favour settlement, but proximity to a river can also expose homes to flooding. A location on slightly higher ground near a usable source may balance access and risk. The best site cannot be selected from distance alone. Water quality, seasonal reliability, ownership and delivery arrangements affect practical access.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.02-01-2",
