    },
    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.02-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Services can reinforce concentration where schools, clinics or shops are located together. They can also be extended to dispersed households through appropriate networks or transport. The cost per user and travel burden vary with spacing and terrain. A settlement label alone does not establish which service design is most efficient. Use distances, population and operation costs where supplied, alongside essential access needs.",
