    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.02-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A schematic example can hold rainfall and household count constant while changing the stated land arrangement. At A, homes are permitted only near a shared service node; at B, each household occupies a separate farm plot. Different arrangements can emerge without a rainfall difference. This helps distinguish a political or tenure mechanism from an invented environmental explanation.",
      "claim_ids": [
