    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.02-19",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A second comparison can hold the land arrangement constant but introduce a narrow usable valley strip at one site. The physical constraint can then help explain alignment, while the other site has more feasible building locations. Even this simplified comparison does not establish every real-world cause. Its purpose is to make a specific mechanism visible and to identify the conditions needed for the explanation.",
      "claim_ids": [
